{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5481-1","published":"2026-11-26T15:26:49Z","modified":"2026-11-27T11:01:29.531907814Z","related":["CVE-2026-107364","CVE-2026-107778","CVE-2026-107884","CVE-2026-112314","CVE-2026-112315","CVE-2026-112316","CVE-2026-112317","CVE-2026-112318","CVE-2026-112319","CVE-2026-112320","CVE-2026-112321","CVE-2026-112322","CVE-2026-112323","CVE-2026-118380","CVE-2026-119079","CVE-2026-71199","CVE-2026-71200"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-107364","CVE-2026-107778","CVE-2026-107884","CVE-2026-112314","CVE-2026-112315","CVE-2026-112316","CVE-2026-112317","CVE-2026-112318","CVE-2026-112319","CVE-2026-112320","CVE-2026-112321","CVE-2026-112322","CVE-2026-112323","CVE-2026-118380","CVE-2026-119079","CVE-2026-71199","CVE-2026-71200"],"summary":"Security update for krb5, krb5-mini","details":"This update for krb5, krb5-mini fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-71199: Alteration of authentication indicators in CAMMAC container (bsc#1290192).\n- CVE-2026-71200: Unauthenticated KDC NULL pointer dereference KDC DoS via crafted PKINIT pre-auth request\n  (bsc#1290193).\n- CVE-2026-107364: Unauthenticated KDC DoS based on ASN.1 decoder read overrun (bsc#1290029).\n- CVE-2026-107778: Denial of service via crafted forwarded credentials (bsc#1284817).\n- CVE-2026-107884: Unauthorized key reset of protected principal via kpasswd (bsc#1290028).\n- CVE-2026-112314: MIT krb5 GSS-RPC client memory leak on XID mismatch retries (bsc#1290050).\n- CVE-2026-112315: kadmind unauthenticated memory leak DoS in RPCSEC_GSS buffer decode failure (bsc#1290176).\n- CVE-2026-112316: kadmind authenticated memory leak DoS in xdr_krb5_tl_data() decode failure (bsc#1290181).\n- CVE-2026-112317: KDC unauthenticated memory leak DoS in KDB keytab key decryption error path (bsc#1290182).\n- CVE-2026-112318: kadmind authenticated DoS exploiting dereference of null policy name pointers (bsc#1290183).\n- CVE-2026-112319: kadmind authenticated memory exhaustion DoS via unbounded RPC XDR allocation (bsc#1290184).\n- CVE-2026-112320: kadmind unauthenticated memory leak DoS via GSS-RPC auth flavor switching (bsc#1290185).\n- CVE-2026-112321: kadmind unauthenticated memory leak DoS via AUTH_GSSAPI_INIT error paths (bsc#1290186).\n- CVE-2026-112322: kadmind unauthenticated CPU DoS via AUTH_GSSAPI client states cleanup (bsc#1290188).\n- CVE-2026-112323: kadmind unauthenticated memory exhaustion via failed AUTH_GSSAPI_INIT requests (bsc#1290189).\n- CVE-2026-118380: kadmind request alteration and protected information disclosure (bsc#1290190).\n- CVE-2026-119079: KDC unauthenticated CPU DoS via quadratic ASN.1 SEQUENCE OF decoding (bsc#1290191).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"krb5","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.3","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/krb5&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"krb5":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:5481-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"krb5","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.4","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/krb5&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"krb5":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:5481-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"krb5","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-ESPOS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/krb5&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-ESPOS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"krb5":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1","krb5-32bit":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1","krb5-client":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1","krb5-devel":"1.19.2-150400.3.29.1"